A||N||12||FieroJoe||Can't stand air fresheners anymore!||||1||
Z||000000||FieroJoe||06-02-2001||09:53 PM||||Well, a turning point has come in my life.  I used to love many different types of Little-tree brand car air fresheners.  Now, I am sad to say, that I just can't stand the smell anymore!<P>The other day, I put a new one in, and a I about hurled from it being so strong, so it was immediatly thrown away.<P>About the only thing that I can have smelling in the car is the car itself.  The vinyl dressing I use smells decent, but it isnt so strong like those air fresheners.  I know they say to leave the baggie on, but that looks so queer!<P>Just thought I would share.  I heard NuVinyl is supposed to smell decent, anyone use it?<P>------------------<BR>  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/joesig_1.jpg"> <BR>'87 Coupe 5spd.<BR>AIM:FieroJoe87||||reg||1
Z||000001||skitime||06-02-2001||11:11 PM||||Never did like them and probably never will.  Whenever I smell them I think a teenage boys trying to coverup cigarette smoke from their parents. Isn't that what they are for?<P>------------------<BR><UL TYPE=SQUARE><BR><LI>Red 88 GT T-TOP<BR><LI>Red 86 GT<BR></UL><BR>      <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/pictures-1_5.jpg"> ||||reg||1
Z||000002||FieroJoe||06-02-2001||11:14 PM||||Well, I originally put them in the car to cover up the previous owner's smoke smell, but now since I have pulled the entire interior and cleaned everything good, the smell is gone.<P>I despise the smell of cigarette smoke.  Sometimes I just feel like yaking when I have to help someone at work who is a heavy smoker.||||reg||1
Z||000003||skitime||06-02-2001||11:36 PM||||I am with you on that one too. Smokers play real havok on car interiors and public surroundings not to mention their personal space.  Please no flames smokers. <P>------------------<BR><UL TYPE=SQUARE><BR><LI>Red 88 GT T-TOP<BR><LI>Red 86 GT<BR></UL><BR>       <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/pictures-1_5.jpg">  <p>[This message has been edited by skitime (edited 06-02-2001).]||||reg||1
Z||000004||sjp777||06-03-2001||12:23 AM||||Well, I'm a pretty light smoker, but I wouldn't even think about lighting up in my car.<P>Fieros have a unique smell all their own. Has anyone else noticed this? They smell different than any other car I have ever had, and it's instantly recognizable.<P>I like it<P>------------------<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/890sm_4.jpg"> <BR>88GT 5sp, in desperate need of an LT1<BR><A HREF="http://www.geocities.com/fiero88gt1/" TARGET=_blank>http://www.geocities.com/fiero88gt1/</A>||||reg||1
Z||000005||fierospeeder||06-03-2001||02:37 AM||||my 87 tbird turbo still had that new car smell.  I think all cars have a distinct odor to them.  My vw and all other bugs have a certain smell also.<P>I had someone that "USE" to be my friend smoke in my car, totally pissed me off, and put a burn mark in the seat when some guy was trying to kick his ass.  in my tbird.  The car doesn't smell like it use to and i dont think i will get the original smell back again. unless i buy another tbird with from a nonsmoker<P>My g/f loves to go to the casino, and i dont gamble.  But anyone that has gone, you know you cant breath at all.  Going outside makes a big difference on your lungs.||||reg||1
Z||000006||JSocha||06-03-2001||04:11 AM||||One of my friends always had the tree freshners hanging in forests from his mirror.<P>However, if you had seen some of the women he dated you would understand the need for em!  Ewwwweeeee! <P>------------------<BR>     <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/jsocha_2.gif"> ||||reg||1
Z||000007||LZeitgeist||06-03-2001||08:57 AM||||Yeah, I can't even buy a car if the seller smoked. Yuck. <P>And *nobody* lights up in any vehicle I own, or place that I live... cigarette smoke just seems to linger FOREVER. Fortunately, my friends know my preference and are very good about this. <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><P><BR>A boss I had a few years ago had this plaque in his office:<P>-------------------------------------------<BR>"I realize that one of the things you like to do is smoke. Now I admit that you have somewhat of a right to smoke if you like. When you light up, your smoke infiltrates the air I breathe, the furniture we sit on, my clothes and my hair.<P>One of the things *I* like to do is drink. Now, you'll have to also admit that I have somewhat of a right to drink if I like. Well, when I drink, one of the side effects is that I have to urinate. So, if you don't mind me urinating all over your furniture, clothes and hair, then by all means, have a smoke."<BR>--------------------------------------------<P>EDIT: typos<p>[This message has been edited by LZeitgeist (edited 06-03-2001).]||||reg||1
Z||000008||SteveJ||06-03-2001||09:51 AM||||Lots of places now have laws against smoking in restaurants, work places, and public gathering places. I live in a county with such laws. You get used to the freedom really fast and come to expect it. When I travel outside it reminds me of how fortunate I am to have such laws here. Smoking in restaurants is the worst most inconsiderate thing anyone can do in polite company.||||reg||1
Z||000009||JSocha||06-03-2001||10:40 AM||||I just tell people in my house and/or my vehicles, <B>"If I see you smoking, I am going to assume you are on fire and put you out!"</B>.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/cool.gif"><P>------------------<BR>     <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/jsocha_2.gif"> ||||reg||12
Z||000010||Tweek||06-03-2001||10:49 AM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by SteveJ:<BR><B>Lots of places now have laws against smoking in restaurants, work places, and public gathering places. I live in a county with such laws. You get used to the freedom really fast and come to expect it. When I travel outside it reminds me of how fortunate I am to have such laws here. Smoking in restaurants is the worst most inconsiderate thing anyone can do in polite company.</B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>Now, I am a light smoker, but I have to say I totaly agree with this. In my state the only building you can smoke in is bars/pool halls and such if the owner agrees, plus if there is such a place 18+ is the ages allowed in. I think smoking around other people wont dont like it, or are eating is just about the rudest, inconsiderate thing you can do. I wish smoking around kids could be considered child abuse. So I only smoke when im outside by myself, or with other smokers. I try to respect other people, simple cause it right.||||reg||1
Z||000011||maryjane||06-03-2001||04:55 PM||||Skitime, I doubt you will get any flame war started over smoking. Most of us would give anything to be able to quit. Stinks up my cars,home, plays havoc with computer screens,not to mention my insides. As far as the pine tree air thingies, I had a job with Kamatsu equipment once, never liked em since. Kamatsu translates into "little pine tree" (It was a crappy job)||||reg||1
Z||000012||Mach10||06-03-2001||08:41 PM||||Tweek: Coming from a fanatical (asthmatic) anti-smoker, you have my complete and total respect. I wish more smokers (light or heavy) were like you.<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><P>||||reg||14
